f Merca\n\nLet $ν_2(m)$ denote the $2$-adic valuation of a positive integer $m$ and set $N_m=m\\bigl(1+ν_2(m)/2\\bigr)$. We prove four conjectures of Merca on the nonnegativity of truncated pentagonal number series weighted by the infinite products $\\prod_{m\\ge 1}(1-q^{2N_m})$ and $\\prod_{r\\ge 1}\\bigl(q^{2^r r};q^{2^{r+1}r}\\bigr)_\\infty$. Our method is to regard the exponent map $m\\mapsto m(ν_2(m)+2)$ as a dynamical system on the positive integers: the factors of the associated quotient link into chains along its forward orbits, and the three orbits seeded at $1$, $4$ and $5$ are pairwise disjoint and telescope to exactly $1/\\bigl((1-q)(1-q^4)(1-q^5)\\bigr)$. The exponent triple $(1,4,5)$ is admissible in the sense of earlier work by Liu, which yields the desired factorization into two series with nonnegative coefficients. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nwhataifound.org: What AI Has Actually Contributed | Registry of AI Scientific & Math Results (https://whataifound.org/?tag=integrality-gap)\nciteturn3search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; The conjecture is layered in $a$: the $a = 2$ layer is classical, containing the Rogers-Ramanujan and Andrews-Gordon identities, and the abstract says nothing was known for $a \\ge 3$. ... number-theory combinatorics q-series lean formalization argument ... Read the arXiv abstracts of arXiv:2608.05480 and of the companion arXiv:2608.15219, and the Lean repository's formalization.yaml, on 2026-10-16. ... Graded claimed because the Lean certificate is explicitly conditional: its formalization.yaml says it proves the implication from eight cited facts, which its source list traces to Schilling, Warnaar, Huang, Andrews and Ramírez Alfonsín, to the paper's Theorem 1.1, so the kernel establishes the deduction rather than the theorem outright, the same structure that keeps 2026-09-17-rogers-ramanujan-torus-knot and 2026-09-02-prime-gaps-186 at claimed.\n## Huang-Jiang-Oblomkov conjecture for a = 3: a new infinite family of Rogers-Ramanujan identities, with a Lean certificate conditional on eight literature facts#\n\nKenny Lau and Ken Ono prove the $a = 3$ layer of the Huang-Jiang-Oblomkov conjecture, which equates a count of commuting nilpotent matrix pairs with $X^3 = Y^b$ over finite fields with an explicit theta quotient, giving a new infinite family of Rogers-Ramanujan identities; AxiomProver produced a Lean certificate of the deduction from eight cited literature facts.\n\nFor coprime $1 < a < b$, Huang, Jiang and Oblomkov assembled the normalized counts of commuting nilpotent $n \\times n$ matrix pairs over $\\mathbb{F}_q$ with $X^a = Y^b$ into a $q$-series $Z_{a,b}(q)$ and conjectured that it equals an explicit product $P_{a,b}(q)$ built from Jacobi's theta function and Dedekind's eta function, which would make the point count essentially a modular function on $\\Gamma(a+b)$. The conjecture is layered in $a$: the $a = 2$ layer is classical, containing the Rogers-Ramanujan and Andrews-Gordon identities, and the abstract says nothing was known for $a \\ge 3$. The registry's 2026-09-17-rogers-ramanujan-torus-knot, which claims every coprime pair, cites this paper as a predecessor; no earlier claim of the $a = 3$ layer was found in the registry. This was not a systematic review of the Rogers-Ramanujan literature, and the year the conjecture was posed is left unrecorded, as on the general entry.\n\nCaveats\n\nGraded claimed because the Lean certificate is explicitly conditional: its formalization.yaml says it proves the implication from eight cited facts, which its source list traces to Schilling, Warnaar, Huang, Andrews and Ramírez Alfonsín, to the paper's Theorem 1.1, so the kernel establishes the deduction rather than the theorem outright, the same structure that keeps 2026-09-17-rogers-ramanujan-torus-knot and 2026-09-02-prime-gaps-186 at claimed. The formal statements were generated by AxiomProver, the system that produced the proofs, and no third party has audited them against the paper; there is no Palomar registration. Autonomy is graded ai-assisted: the abstract, and the paper as vibemathed quotes it, place AxiomProver on the certificate only, and the mathematics is the authors'. Only the abstract was read for this entry, not the paper. The result is contained in the general case claimed a month later by an overlapping author group; it is entered separately as the first case beyond the classical $a = 2$ layer to be claimed. Unrefereed.\n\nOriginal work\n\narXiv Lau and Ono, Modularity of Point Counts for the Curves Xᵃ = Yᵇ: New Rogers-Ramanujan Identities↗GitHub AxiomMath/RR_a3, the conditional Lean certificate↗arXiv Huang, Lau, Ono and Paule, Algebraic geometric framework of Rogers-Ramanujan identities, the companion cases↗\n\nIN Independent\n\n2026-08-05\n\nFormally verified Collaborative\n\nModel\n    GPT-5.6 Pro\n\nField\n    mathematics\n\nPosed\n    1959 · open 67 yrs\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTheoretical computer science: AI research tracker · AI Proof Watch (https://aiproofwatch.com/problems/theoretical-computer-science)\nciteturn3search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; arXiv:2609.03065v1 Paper date: 2 Sept 2026 ... ### A counterexample to the stable forking conjecture ... Freitag and Mutchnik give a stable theory of an infinite-dimensional vector space over the division ring of fractions of the quantum graph algebra of the random graph, refuting stable forking. ... ### On supporting affine functionals for Entanglement of Formation\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOATI - 2024 - Rapport annuel d'activité (https://radar.inria.fr/report/2024/coati/index.html)\nciteturn3search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ##### Distinguishing labelling problems and the 1-2-3 Conjecture ... A proof of the 1-2-3 Conjecture has been provided recently, in 2024, by Keusch.\n----------